x86_64-linux  two differences, neither about names. clang zeroes the `Nested()` temporary with a call to memset where cxx1 writes the fields out - which for a compiler that ships no runtime is the answer it has to give, and is why `memset` appears on clang's side and nothing on cxx1's. And WithCtor's constructor is written inside its class, so clang emits one comdat copy as C2 and no C1 where cxx1 emits both of Itanium's forms - see docs/CONFORMANCE.md, "An inline member function is a strong symbol"
x86_64-windows  the memset half of the same, on this ABI. arm64-darwin agrees with clang on all 5 names, clang having chosen stores there rather than a call - which is the point: what a compiler zeroes with is its own business, and both zero
